  "name": "Periodic damage grants Hourglass of Eternity's haste (#1294)",
  "contract": "Hourglass of Eternity 806337 applies aura 42 (proc trigger spell) on 504726, a 5 s self-buff of aura 216 (SPELL_AURA_HASTE_SPELLS, BasePoints 24 = +25%) that is native in AuraEffect::HandleModCastingSpeed, but Spell.dbc gives 806337 ProcFlags 0, so SpellMgr::LoadSpellProcs generated no entry and Aura::GetProcEffectMask returned 0 for every tick. Its tooltip is \"Periodic damage dealt now has a $h% chance to grant you 25% increased haste for 5 sec\", with $h = the record's own ProcChance of 5. ACHIEVED FALSE-FAILURE PROBABILITY: 5.4%. The buff lives only 5000 ms (duration index 28), so a trial only counts if it happens while the assertion is polling; ticks produced by earlier steps have expired by then. The scenario therefore opens as many concurrent DoTs as the harness allows and then polls: eight Decomposition DoTs (Amplitude 4000, duration index 86 = 21000 ms) give 27 ticks inside the window, Melt Reality (Amplitude 4000, duration index 325 = 36000 ms) gives 6, Timerend (Amplitude 1000, duration index 32 = 6000 ms) gives 5, three self-cast DoT fixtures on the caster give 15 and a final Unmake (Amplitude 250, duration index 36 = 1000 ms) gives 4, for 57 independent trials: 0.95^57 = 0.054. That is above the 1% the batch aims for and cannot be improved inside this harness - eight creatures is the maximum, Melt Reality and Timerend carry 30 s and 20 s cooldowns, Unmake's 1000 ms DoT cannot overlap its own 1500 ms cast, and there is no haste fixture - so a failure of this scenario should be re-run once before it is believed. The real 5% chance is not lowered.",
